agent-tools (1.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * claude-user: add diagnose, which lists each config dir's projects
    with the account each belongs to, and reports missing or logged-out
    accounts, shared logins, misplaced projects and unused
    ~/.claude-NAME dirs.
  * claude-user: add login, which runs claude auth login as an account
    from an empty temporary directory.
  * claude-sync: split --all moves a project with no transcripts, such
    as one holding only memory, by matching its name to an existing
    directory.

 -- Christopher Hoover <ch@murgatroid.com>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:25:26 -0700

agent-tools (1.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * claude-user (new): run Claude Code as the account (work, personal, ...)
    a directory belongs to, each with its own CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR.
    ~/.config/claude-user/config maps directories to accounts; the longest
    match wins.
  * claude-sync: sync and mv work on one account's Claude dir, the
    project's or --account's; the peer maps the account name with its own
    config.
  * claude-sync: add split, which moves projects' sessions, session data,
    prompts and settings to the account they belong to; split --all sorts
    a ~/.claude that held every account.
  * agent-ps: look up sessions in every account's sessions/ and show an
    ACCOUNT column when any session's account is known.
  * agent-install (new): print the command that installs Claude Code, Codex
    or Antigravity CLI from the vendor's native installer, run so it leaves
    shell startup files alone.
  * Install the scripts under /usr/lib/agent-tools, with /usr/bin symlinks,
    so they can import each other.

 -- Christopher Hoover <ch@murgatroid.com>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 19:16:10 -0700

agent-tools (1.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * claude-sync: add mv, which renames a project directory and updates
    Claude Code's records of it (project dirs, transcript cwds,
    history.jsonl, ~/.claude.json) so its sessions still resume.

 -- Christopher Hoover <ch@murgatroid.com>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 09:47:02 -0700

agent-tools (1.1.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * claude-sync: stop when a session record can't be read, instead of
    treating that session as closed and syncing it while it runs.
  * claude-sync: stop when a file or directory can't be scanned, instead of
    treating it as deleted.
  * claude-sync: save the sync base on the peer before saving it locally, so
    a failed push can't make a later edit on the peer look unchanged.
  * claude-sync: chain diverged transcripts onto the leaf --resume continues
    from, put a compacted tail first, split on newlines only, and make
    re-merging idempotent.
  * claude-sync: merge history.jsonl and MEMORY.md on newlines only; a prompt
    containing U+2028 was split in two and corrupted the history on both
    machines.
  * claude-sync: refuse machine ids that could be paths, give each trash
    operation its own directory, don't purge trash on a dry run, and make
    rsync copy every file it is given.

 -- Christopher Hoover <ch@murgatroid.com>  Sun, 11 Oct 2026 11:54:58 -0700

agent-tools (1.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * claude-sync: write merged transcripts, conflict copies and its own state
    owner-only (0600); they were created with the umask and could be read by
    other users.
  * claude-sync: refuse file paths from the peer that would leave ~/.claude,
    and never copy symlinks.

 -- Christopher Hoover <ch@murgatroid.com>  Sun, 11 Oct 2026 10:57:49 -0700

agent-tools (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * claude-sync: new tool. Two-way sync of Claude Code sessions between two
    machines over ssh and rsync, so a session can be resumed on either one.
    A session continued on both machines is chained into one conversation,
    with both originals kept as conflict copies.

 -- Christopher Hoover <ch@murgatroid.com>  Sun, 11 Oct 2026 10:49:36 -0700

